 "caveats": "Line 3 'kept them pecking fast and steadily' reflects standard VR-schedule findings; avoid stronger claims like 'most addictive schedule'. The slot-machine analogy for phones is a design critique (Brichter, Tristan Harris) and a plausible mechanism, not a proven equivalence; Lindström 2021 shows reward-learning patterns in posting, not addiction. Verify the Brichter quote against the Guardian article itself (Wikipedia used as pointer). The 1957 visual is the book's publication year; the research ran through the 1950s. Round-4 edit: quote marks removed from 'problematic use' in the narration text (caption artefact); 'say' respells Ferster as FUR-stir. Round-5 edit: narration credits 'Skinner's lab' (Ferster & Skinner 1957, Schedules of Reinforcement) instead of naming Ferster, which TTS garbled.",
